{"title":"Siddha Drug Consultant Roadmap","role":"Siddha Drug Consultant","summary":"A Siddha Drug Consultant applies knowledge of Siddha medicine, medicinal plants, formulations, pharmacology, quality considerations, traditional pharmaceutics and patient-care principles to support the appropriate selection, formulation, documentation, quality evaluation or professional use of Siddha medicines.","facts":{"Current degree":"BSMS (Siddha)","Course":"Siddha Medicine & Surgery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Siddha Drug Consultant applies knowledge of Siddha medicine, medicinal plants, formulations, pharmacology, quality considerations, traditional pharmaceutics and patient-care principles to support the appropriate selection, formulation, documentation, quality evaluation or professional use of Siddha medicines."},{"type":"p","text":"A BSMS graduate has a broader Siddha medical foundation, while a drug-focused career can move toward Siddha pharmacy, formulation development, quality control, research, regulatory affairs, pharmacovigilance, manufacturing and clinical support."},{"type":"h","text":"Potential work environments include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Siddha hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Siddha pharmacies"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH institutions"},{"type":"h","text":"Siddha pharmaceutical companies"},{"type":"h","text":"Herbal medicine manufacturers"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality-control laboratories"},{"type":"h","text":"Research institutions"},{"type":"h","text":"Drug-regulatory organizations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic institutions"},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional medicine product companies"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Siddha Drug Consultant” is not necessarily a single statutory professional designation. The exact authority to prescribe, manufacture, formulate, dispense, test or certify medicines depends on the professi